.DS_Store

# Finder / iCloud duplicate-copy artifacts of the .ino sketch, e.g.
# "m32_v6.ino 2.cpp" — these cause "multiple definition" link errors.
# (A pre-build hook, scripts/clean_ino_dupes.py, also strips them.)
*.ino [0-9]*.cpp

# Audio-accessibility (V9.0): the TTS clips under Software/src/data/voice/ ARE
# committed. They look like build artifacts but are not reproducible from a clean
# clone -- the Piper voice model below is gitignored -- so ignoring them left the
# accessibility edition silently mute for anyone else who built it. Committing
# them also means a builder who just wants to flash needs no TTS toolchain, only
# `-t uploadfs`. Filenames are md5(spoken text), so clips are immutable and new
# UI text only ever adds files; `generate_audio.sh --prune` clears orphans.

# Audio-accessibility tooling: Piper venv + voice models (machine-specific / large)
Software/tools/audio-accessibility/.venv/
Software/tools/audio-accessibility/models/
__pycache__/

# Per-variant manuals (Documentation/User Manual/Version <N>.x/). The combined
# manual -- m32UserManual_v<N>_{en,de}.pdf and manual_{en,de}.html -- is still
# committed as before; the classic / pocket / pocket-a11y builds are produced on
# demand by "./build.sh all pdf all" and are not committed while the decision
# on what the release ships is still open.
Documentation/User Manual/Version */m32UserManual_v*_??_*.pdf
Documentation/User Manual/Version */manual_??_*.html
Documentation/User Manual/Version */m32UserManual_v*.epub

# iOS config app (Software/iOS/M32Config). These rules live HERE rather than in
# a .gitignore inside the app directory because a per-directory .gitignore
# travels with its branch: checking out a branch that predates the app leaves
# its build output behind as untracked files, one `git add .` away from being
# committed to the wrong branch. Scoped to the app's path so an unrelated
# build/ or DerivedData/ elsewhere in the tree is unaffected.
Software/iOS/M32Config/M32Config.xcodeproj/
Software/iOS/M32Config/Generated/
Software/iOS/M32Config/build/
Software/iOS/M32Config/DerivedData/
Software/iOS/M32Config/**/xcuserdata/
Software/iOS/M32Config/**/*.xcuserstate

# Copied out of Software/Utilities by sync-webtool.sh at build time -- the tool
# there is the single source of truth. bridge.js sits in the same directory and
# IS committed.
Software/iOS/M32Config/Resources/Web/m32_config_tool.html
Software/iOS/M32Config/Resources/Web/m32_pref_help.json
